            "review_text": "Andy G\nBangkok, Thailand195 contributions\n0\nExpensive & Pretentious\nApr 2017 • Couples\nNever forget the most important thing about any restaurant is THE FOOD. We were looking for another restaurant recommended by TA but couldn't find so we stumbled on theis one. It looked quite slick from outside - sexy lighting and banks of wine bottle all stacked up in a rack as you walk in. Waitresses English was limited but she tried her best. The menu looked very impressive - we were licking our lips !! My baked salmon was good but a little overcooked. The green salad and balsamic never arrived neither did my wife's fried rice. Her crap in tamarind sauce was nice - but we were both hungry and in desperate need of a fix of carbs - where's the effin rice got to? It turned up just as the last mouthful of crab was disappearing down Nids gullet - not good news. My french fries were so thin that there was no discernible potato left inside them - bad news for someone eager for a carb fix. I asked the manager to come and talk to me after we'd finished so as to offer some constructive criticism - she listened and nodded obligingly but I have my doubts as to whether my comments really hit home. A 5% discount was a gesture - but no more than that. The damage had already been done. It's a bit like a government offering you a million dollars coz they accidentally wiped out your farm and half your family - completely unsatisfactory. My advice has to be give this place a miss.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 15, 2017",
