            "review_text": "fkhavarpour\nSydney, Australia1 contribution\n0\n\"failing to get a good service\"\nOct 2016 • Friends\nWe attended this restaurant, with a large group of people interested in having a good Vietnamese food. The restaurant is located in a well-established neighbourhood close to the Reconciliation palace. Although is a nicely decorated, with multi-levels of dinning services, still the service was less than what is was expected from such a decorated establishment. Four of us, sitting in the middle of a long table [23 people all together] did not receive our predetermined food for a long time. We requested to be served, but our request was ignored in the first time. We had to raise the issues again with the waitresses and after a long discussion, due to lack of English proficiency by the staff, we were finally served, like other members of the group. It seems restaurant has a policy on the number of food proportion allocated to each table, regardless of number of people present to receive the service. To finalise, the food was mediocre and the service was lousy to the say the list.\nRead more\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 5, 2016",
